  "system": {
    "source": {
      "custom": "",
      "book": "RAINTDM",
      "page": "",
      "license": "",
      "rules": "2024",
      "revision": 1
    },
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>The hammer is a powerful blunt weapon with a surprising amount of mobility. It's also possible to stun monsters by delivering a hammer attack to the head.</p><p><a href=\"https://amellwind-mh-dn-d5e-foundry-toolbox-2.vercel.app/weapons?weapon=Hammer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Hammer in the Toolbox</a></p><hr><h3>Features</h3><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Mastery Property (Topple)</strong></p><p>If you hit a creature, you can force it to make a Constitution saving throw (DC 8 + your Proficiency Bonus + your Strength modifier). On a failed save, the creature has the Prone condition.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Power Charge</strong></p><p><strong>Bonus Action.</strong></p><p>As a Bonus Action, you begin winding up the hammer. The weapon remains charged for 1 minute, until you hit with an attack using it, until you are knocked Prone or your are incapacitated. While charged, your walking speed increases by 5 feet, and your next successful attack with this weapon deals an extra [[/r 1d6]] bludgeoning damage.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Charge Upgrade I</strong></p><p>Your Power Charge now deals an extra [[/r 2d6]] bludgeoning damage on a hit.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Upswing / Spinning Bludgeon</strong></p><p>Your charged attacks gain tactical versatility. When you hit a creature with an attack empowered by your Power Charge, you can choose one of the following additional effects:</p><p>Upswing: The target is pushed 10 feet away from you. If they hit a solid object (like a wall or another creature), they take an additional [[/r 1d6]] bludgeoning damage.</p><p>Spinning Bludgeon: You carry the momentum into a spin. Choose a second creature within 5 feet of the original target; you can immediately make one melee weapon attack against the second creature (this second attack does not benefit from the charge's extra damage).</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Charge Upgrade II</strong></p><p>Your Power Charge now deals an extra [[/r 3d6]] bludgeoning damage on a hit.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Mighty Weapon</strong></p><p>When you hit a creature that is Large or smaller with this weapon, you can choose to have it make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your proficiency + your Strength modifier. On a failed save the creature is stunned until the end of your next turn. Once used, you can't use this property again until you finish a short or long rest.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Stun Upgrade</strong></p><p>Creatures of Huge or Gargantuan size no longer have Advantage on the saving throw against your Concussive Blow.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Offset Smash</strong></p><p><strong>Reaction.</strong></p><p>You can use the hammer's momentum to power through an enemy's guard. If a creature within your reach misses you with a melee attack, you can use your Reaction to immediately make one attack against them. If your weapon was affected by Power Charge, this reaction attack gains the charge's benefits and you have Advantage on the attack roll.</p></div>",
      "chat": "<p>The hammer is a powerful blunt weapon with a surprising amount of mobility. It's also possible to stun monsters by delivering a hammer attack to the head.</p><hr><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Mastery Property (Topple)</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Power Charge</strong></p><p><strong>Bonus Action.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Charge Upgrade I</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Upswing / Spinning Bludgeon</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Charge Upgrade II</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Mighty Weapon</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Stun Upgrade</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Offset Smash</strong></p><p><strong>Reaction.</strong></p></div>"
    },
